Package: lcos-bootmenu
Version: 1.1.0-1
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 908
Maintainer: LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>
Homepage: https://lunduke.com
Depends: grub-common, grub-efi-amd64-bin, refind (>= 0.14.2)
Recommends: efibootmgr, grub-efi-ia32-bin
Description: LCOS 1.1 boot menu (rEFInd picker, GRUB theme)
 Mac-style boot menu for LCOS 1.1. On a new UEFI install, Calamares runs
 lcos-bootmenu after GRUB and rEFInd becomes the picker: big OS icons,
 mouse, a 5 second timeout, and the last choice remembered on the EFI
 system partition. The LCOS tile chainloads the install's GRUB, which
 stays hidden (timeout 0) and still does cryptodisk, $lcos_quirks and
 kernel updates. "Boot options" on that tile (or holding Shift) opens
 GRUB's menu, including older kernels.
 .
 BIOS installs and the live ISO use the same navy GRUB theme (DejaVu,
 logo, OS icons). The package does not install rEFInd from its
 maintainer scripts, so an upgrade from 1.0.x does not change the boot
 partition until lcos-bootmenu install is run.
 .
 Secure Boot is not supported. The Lunduke kernel is unsigned, and this
 package does not install shim or a Machine Owner Key.
